    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Open">Review step</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Apps">1. Choose your applications</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_AppsHint">Replace the sample with your applications, or add an open window. Check each path, website address and startup option.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Access">2. Protect configuration changes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_AccessHint">Set an administrator PIN and a session timeout. Add an operator PIN and scope if needed. Keep a separate Windows administrator recovery route before enabling kiosk mode.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Browsers">3. Connect websites</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_BrowsersHint">For managed websites, install the browser connection and pair the intended profile. Refresh the connection status, then test switching to the same tab twice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Workspace">4. Arrange your workspace</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_WorkspaceHint">Open the applications, arrange their windows and save a workspace if useful. Check the selected monitor and restore it once.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Backups">5. Keep a recovery copy</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_BackupsHint">Save your settings and export a backup to a safe location. Review the restore preview and test recovery on a spare installation. Encrypted configuration belongs to this Windows account.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Test">6. Check daily operation</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_TestHint">Launch and switch each application, check keyboard and touch access, test an offline restart, and review monitoring. Test kiosk entry and its exit route on a spare workstation before deployment.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Browser_RepairReady">Use the website's switch test to verify that the intended tab is activated.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Browser_RepairJournal">Close AppSwitcher and preserve its data folder. Restore a known-good browser ownership journal with your administrator's help. Do not delete the journal or reset identities to force a new tab.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Browser_RepairUrl">Review the website address. Use an http or https address without an embedded username or password.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Browser_RepairAbsent">The managed website is closed. Use Open in the launcher when you want to start it again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Browser_RepairProfileConflict">Close the copied browser profile. Open only the original paired profile and refresh. Keep its profile identity; do not create another website entry.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Browser_RepairIdentity">Restore the original AppSwitcher tab group and leave one managed tab for this application, then refresh. Do not repeatedly launch or duplicate the entry while its identity is uncertain.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Browser_RepairInvalidIdentity">Restore a known-good configuration backup. Application IDs identify managed tabs; do not hand-edit them or reuse an ID for another entry.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Browser_RepairProfileChanged">Reconnect the previous profile and close the managed website through AppSwitcher. Then choose the new profile in the website settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Browser_RepairPairing">Choose Setup, open the intended browser profile and approve the AppSwitcher extension. Select that connected profile for the website, then refresh.</sys:String>

